  "by": "AI (Claude), 2026-09-26, from reports/stage5/export_review.png and reports/stage5/valdris_board.png",
  "judgement": [
   "The shipped file is the stage-4 file: in all seven review shots the re-imported valdris.glb with the colossus_cannon on the imported weapon_R matches the stage-4 source render pose for pose (clip pose error <= 2.7e-5 m over all 34 clips); the textures from inside the GLB, the emissive seams and the single-sided material all read as in the source.",
   "The cannon sits on the right forearm through every shot and rides weapon_R through the heavy shot (5.4e-7); nothing of the sleeve weapon is lost in the export.",
   "At game size (160 px at 22 m, 1080p) he reads as the widest, heaviest body in the roster: the pauldron blocks, the cannon's glowing muzzle and the red cape; the head is the small dark knot of the concept.",
   "Against the concept the gap is the stage-2 look, not the export: the plate edges carry a bright gold trim on every piece, so the armour reads boxier and busier than the concept's dark forged bronze; the anvil reads as a flat light-grey wedge where the concept's is dark iron; the cape is a plain red panel without the concept's tatters and emblem. These are for the user's final visual approval (the Hades-II bar), not fixable in stage 5."
  ],
  "not_checked": "No Bevy-side load: the Rust test that loads the GLB through bevy_gltf, spawns #Scene0 and plays each clip belongs to the engine integration (crates/). The review renders are the Cycles-CPU toon preview, not the game's shading."
 },
